{
  "comment": "task recipe-data-b1 — the RM.Press lamp/TNT walks (Loader_Recipes_Vanilla.java:776-799 verbatim). Family expansion is the PORT-universe subset of the upstream ANY groups: ANY.Glowstone = {Glowstone, Gloomstone} (the 5 planet glowstones are the GC-compat faces absent from the port material tree) and ANY.SiO2 = {SiO2, NetherQuartz, CertusQuartz, Quartzite}. The ST.tag(1) selector legs are DROPPED — the JSON v1 row schema carries no damage/NBT faces and the configured Integrated Circuit is not expressible as a plain item id (the loom.json precedent; declared deviation: the rows answer without the circuit). DECLARED B2/POOL: the bullet-casing rows (Loader_Recipes_Other.java:657-668 — their mold input is size-0 not-consumable, a face the JSON v1 row schema does not carry either; the molds are registered by task explosives-chain), the food-mold event rows (Loader_Recipes_Food.java:146-152), the :254-259 bullet retips (the round/bolt walk onto the blank bulletGt{Small,Medium,Large} of MT.Empty — the Or(PROJECTILES, EMPTY) carriers make them pourable but the pool card owns them) and the electrode station walk reference port-absent items or per-material rule walks, neither is a static JSON row face. Task toolhead-r11e-press-mortar reclaimed the tool-head statements as ONE representative row per upstream walk (the mortar.json :705-706 Blaze convention): :247-250 (the ANY.Iron raw/finished pickaxe-head bases, Diamond gem / Iron base representatives) and :252-253 (the arrow retips onto the plain Empty arrows). Task toolhead-family-closeout reclaims the :251 Empty-pickaxeGem-head retip — the OP.java:621 force row landed in GTMaterialItems.forceItemGeneration so the blank head exists, and the GT_Tool_PickaxeGem.java:30 drop ring returns exactly this blank: break -> blank -> press with 2 flawed gems -> new head. Still POOLED: the Shape_Extruder_Empty mold-synthesis chain (a crafting-table band, MultiItemTechnological.java:184-222 — zero Empty rows exist in the upstream extruder map, so extruder.json carries none; the r11c pooled face). Task explosives-chain reclaims the dynamite/boomstick rows (Loader_Recipes_Other.java:641-655): the ANY.SiO2 walk is the 4-statement x 4-port-member expansion (:642-645) plus the four Dynamite (:647-650) and four Dynamite_Strong (:652-655) rows — the same ST.tag selector-leg drop as the b1 rows above (the dust amounts 1-vs-2 keep the two families non-colliding without the circuit).",
